WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.314
Welcome to OurWater.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:07.474
After this video you will be able to choose
your place, read the weather for your week,

00:00:07.594 --> 00:00:10.570
and see how much water your crops may need.

00:00:11.383 --> 00:00:14.623
Before you walk to the field, look at the sky.

00:00:14.743 --> 00:00:17.647
On your Home page, choose My weather.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.490
This is the Weather page.

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:24.402
It shows one place at a time, and you choose
the place.

00:00:24.522 --> 00:00:27.186
My weather is also in the menu.

00:00:28.017 --> 00:00:31.185
This grey line shows the place you are looking
at.

00:00:31.305 --> 00:00:33.177
Read it first.

00:00:33.297 --> 00:00:37.377
It starts at the place saved in Settings, here
Badgaon.

00:00:38.183 --> 00:00:43.439
Beside it, one menu called Change location
gives three ways to set your place.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.498
First, Use current location asks your phone
where you are.

00:00:48.618 --> 00:00:51.810
If you say no, you see this red line.

00:00:52.617 --> 00:00:55.209
Second, Enter coordinates.

00:00:55.329 --> 00:00:59.529
Type the latitude and longitude of your well,
then press Go.

00:00:59.649 --> 00:01:02.481
A station's page shows both numbers.

00:01:03.283 --> 00:01:08.707
If a number cannot be right, like a latitude
above ninety, OurWater tells you.

00:01:09.517 --> 00:01:11.869
Correct the number and press Go.

00:01:11.989 --> 00:01:14.821
The line now shows the numbers you typed.

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:19.370
Third, and easiest: Search for a place.

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:21.434
Type your village name.

00:01:21.554 --> 00:01:23.618
Here we type Badgaon.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:27.162
Each match shows the state and country.

00:01:27.282 --> 00:01:31.986
Several places share one name, so read the
state before you choose.

00:01:32.817 --> 00:01:34.689
Choose the right one.

00:01:34.809 --> 00:01:38.817
The line changes to Badgaon, and the whole
page follows.

00:01:38.937 --> 00:01:41.577
The place is saved on this device.

00:01:42.383 --> 00:01:45.287
Now four boxes show the weather right now.

00:01:46.117 --> 00:01:49.381
Temperature: how hot the air is at this
moment.

00:01:50.183 --> 00:01:53.519
Relative humidity: how damp the air is.

00:01:53.639 --> 00:01:57.311
Dry air takes water from soil and leaves
faster.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:03.013
Rain shows what is falling now, and under it
the total expected today.

00:02:03.817 --> 00:02:10.945
The last box is how thirsty the air is today: the water a
healthy green crop would lose to sun and wind in one day.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:13.910
This box is for farmers.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:19.262
It adds up the next seven days, and shows how
much water your crops may need from you.

00:02:20.083 --> 00:02:24.427
First line: the water your crops are expected
to use this week.

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:29.906
Second line: all the rain the forecast expects
in the same days.

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:34.437
Third line: only the rain that really soaks
in.

00:02:34.557 --> 00:02:39.381
Small showers dry up, and heavy rain runs off,
so this is smaller.

00:02:40.183 --> 00:02:44.191
The last line is the answer: water you may
need to add.

00:02:44.311 --> 00:02:47.623
Here it is zero, so rain should be enough.

00:02:47.743 --> 00:02:50.167
In a dry week, it grows.

00:02:50.983 --> 00:02:54.007
At the top right of this box is a question
mark.

00:02:54.127 --> 00:02:57.055
Press it to see how the numbers are worked
out.

00:02:57.883 --> 00:03:01.387
A short explanation opens, in three rules.

00:03:02.217 --> 00:03:06.825
Rule one: up to five millimetres of rain in a
day counts for nothing.

00:03:06.945 --> 00:03:11.769
Above five, three quarters of the extra
counts, up to twenty-five.

00:03:12.583 --> 00:03:15.463
Rules two and three add up the week.

00:03:15.583 --> 00:03:20.407
Net need is crop water minus counted rain,
never below zero.

00:03:21.217 --> 00:03:23.137
These are predictions.

00:03:23.257 --> 00:03:26.113
They may change when the forecast updates.

00:03:26.917 --> 00:03:28.789
Press Close.

00:03:28.909 --> 00:03:32.725
Now the seven day outlook, one row for each
day.

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:36.550
Today's row is shaded and says Today.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:41.334
High and Low: the hottest and coolest
temperature that day.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:45.870
Rain: millimetres expected to fall that day.

00:03:46.683 --> 00:03:51.363
Effective rain: the part that counts for
crops, by the rules we read.

00:03:52.183 --> 00:03:56.815
E T zero: the water sun and wind will take
from a field that day.

00:03:57.617 --> 00:04:00.113
The last column is a running total.

00:04:00.233 --> 00:04:03.713
Its last number is the crop water use in the
box above.

00:04:04.517 --> 00:04:08.213
Remember, these are predictions, not
measurements.

00:04:08.333 --> 00:04:10.613
A storm can miss your field.

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:14.153
Your own rain gauge tells the truth.

00:04:14.273 --> 00:04:17.537
After rain, compare it with this Rain number.

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:20.609
If they differ often, trust your gauge.

00:04:21.417 --> 00:04:24.441
Your place is remembered on this device.

00:04:24.561 --> 00:04:27.273
Units follow your choice in Settings.

00:04:28.083 --> 00:04:30.051
That is the Weather page.

00:04:30.171 --> 00:04:35.283
Check the place first, read the week, and
trust your own rain gauge most.

00:04:35.403 --> 00:04:38.067
Thanks for helping look after our water.
